_to_delete/

# Screen captures taken while iterating on the design (before/after comparison
# material). Working artefacts of a session, not repository content.
scratch_*.png

# Operational compose override, machine-local. Stage 3B.2 adoption keeps the
# runtime on the legacy `avelren` DSN (adopt.sh restarts clients "on the
# UNCHANGED legacy DSN"; the per-role DSN cutover is the separate 3C gate). On a
# host that is mid-rollout — un-adopted, or where a rolled-back adoption revoked
# the per-role grants — the tracked compose's per-role DSNs cannot connect, so
# the operator (or adopt.sh) supplies a legacy-DSN override here. It must NOT be
# committed (it is host state), and it must NOT dirty the worktree: the adoption
# clean-worktree guard would otherwise refuse to run while the override that
# keeps the site up is present. Removed at the 3C cutover.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Local build output (APKs, etc.) copied here by hand for distribution —
# never a build artifact the repo should track.
dist/

# Zipped export staged for Claude Design (DesignSync). Derived from
# design-system/ — that directory IS tracked: it is the ROAD SIGN source of
# truth the Compose code is written against, and it must survive this machine.
design-system.zip
_architect/
